   "whatUniqueZeroMeans": "every commit that locales would remove is also removed by another segment, so dropping locales alone cannot move the column by even one commit. generated is the only segment on twenty large enough to account for that overlap; that it does account for it is consistent with the figures and is not separately measured here."
  },
  "causeEstablished": "the prediction was wrong, but not for the reason (a) named. locales is not a segment without bite on twenty: it would remove 995 commits of 12759 on its own. It has no UNIQUE bite. The check is not blind: on twenty, build has unique 11, generated 4, i18n 1 and translations 1, so a drop-one-out perturbation of any of those would move the column.",
  "checkPowerOnTwenty": {
   "build": 11,
   "generated": 4,
   "i18n": 1,
   "translations": 1,
   "note": "only build is at or above ten; the others are reported as raw figures and no conclusion is drawn from them individually"
  },
  "theRationaleQuestion": {
   "conditionTheOwnerNamed": "if the locale segments measure zero on twenty, the pre-registrations stated rationale and its measured mechanism are not the same thing",
   "conditionOccurred": false,
   "why": "selector-b.md point 2 cites 47 of 224 pre-screen positives as generated locale files. locales measures 1072 touches and 995 removes_alone on twenty, so locale files are abundantly present and would remove commits. The rationale is NOT contradicted and no edit to selector-b.md is owed. What is true instead, and is new, is that on twenty the contribution of locales is wholly redundant with another segment."
